  "body": "Between 2026-11-11 and 2026-11-21, workspace integration test binaries grew from 412 to 1,020 (`crates/app/tests/` grew from 267 to 622). Only one directory suite (`crates/motion/tests/rest_adaptive/main.rs`) exists even though `#927` shipped.\n\nEach integration test binary in `camcraft-app` takes about 103.5 MB on Linux (about 100 MB with `.pdb` on Windows, `docs/decisions/3169-gate-unit-sweep.md`). One target set uses 82.07 GB for integration binaries out of 83.89 GB total.\n\nAdd the fourth rule from #919 Q5 to `AGENTS.md` (\"Testing\" and \"Code shape\") and to the PR-review checklist:\n- Add a new integration test to an existing domain directory suite (`tests/<suite>/<submod>.rs`) before creating a new top-level binary.\n- Exempt `ISOLATED` (`xtask/src/lanes.rs`) and `SLOW_BINARIES` (`xtask/src/plan.rs`) suites, which must stay separate binaries.\n- A new top-level integration test file requires a one-line reason in the PR body.\n\nWait for the `xtask` directory-suite prerequisite (Part of #919) so `assets.rs` and `quick.rs` handle directory suites before the rule takes effect.\n\nEvidence and measurements: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/919#issuecomment-7065686766\n\nDone means: `AGENTS.md` and the PR-review checklist state the rule and its exemptions, and the PR body includes `Process change: yes`.\n\nPart of #919\n",
